{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Goal\n\nRemove the deprecated **legacy `rebar reconcile` CLI command** — specifically its `--mode reconcile-check` legacy route and the legacy-only `--filter-local-ids` flag — and migrate every caller to the canonical `rebar bridge` surface. Approved cleanup (removal; no hard-error/deprecation-shim required — very few clients, none expected to use these).\n\n## Scope (files edited/removed — explicit)\n\nCLI surface removal:\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py` — remove the legacy `reconcile` route registration.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/reconcile.py` — remove the legacy reconcile parser (incl. `--filter-local-ids`).\n- `src/rebar/_cli/help/reconcile.txt` — remove the legacy reconcile help text.\n\nEngine legacy-route removal:\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mode.py` — remove `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py` — remove `_run_reconcile_check`, its `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` writer, the `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` dispatch branch, and residual `--filter-local-ids` wiring on the legacy route.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py` — remove the legacy-route `--filter-local-ids` parsing and its \"available only on the legacy route\" guard; PRESERVE canonical bridge-verb normalization.\n\nCaller migration to the canonical op:\n- `src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py` — repoint `MODE_COMMANDS[\"reconcile-check\"]` from `(\"rebar\",\"reconcile\",\"--mode\",\"reconcile-check\")` to the canonical **`(\"rebar\",\"bridge\",\"fsck\")`** (Design Decision 3).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py` — preserve `reconcile_diagnostics` surfacing via the canonical path (Design Decision 3 / AC4).\n- `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`, `Jenkinsfile` — migrate the invocation to the canonical op (the `reconcile-check` PROFILE/mode label MAY be retained as a compatibility spelling; only the underlying invocation changes).\n- `scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2e_field_validation_probe.sh`, `scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2e_validation_probe.sh` — migrate `run_reconciler --mode reconcile-check` invocations.\n\nDocs/tests:\n- `docs` — document the removal + canonical migration path.\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — record removal.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` — held-out oracle + regression tests.\n\n## Design Decisions (resolve plan-review BLOCK findings)\n\n**1. `--filter-local-ids` (finding 1).** This flag is legacy-route-only (`request.py`: \"available only on the legacy route\"). Its CLI surface removal (parser, help, request.py parsing) is IN SCOPE here and captured by AC1. The now-dead engine-internal `filter_local_ids` plumbing (which defaults `None` once the legacy route is gone, collapsing every `selection_ids or filter_local_ids` fallback to `selection_ids`) is DEFERRED to follow-up **f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0** (versicolor-needless-jackal, linked `discovered_from`) to keep this change bounded.\n\n**2. `_ref_lock.py` LIVE pause sentinel (finding 2).** The string `\"reconcile-check\"` ALSO appears in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py` as a LIVE pause-schema sentinel (`gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"`; `_PAUSE_FIELDS`; strict decode; encode; CAS). This is SEMANTICALLY DISTINCT from the removed CLI command and from the historical `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` report — it is live pause state that AC requires remain unchanged. **DECISION: PRESERVE `_ref_lock.py` BYTE-FOR-BYTE**; do NOT edit pause encode/decode/CAS. `_ref_lock.py` is intentionally NOT in the edit set. AC3 requires a regression test proving a paused ref-lock blob still strict-decodes and CAS-advances after the CLI removal.\n\n**3. Canonical replacement op + diagnostic provenance (finding 3).** The legacy `reconcile-check` mode was the SOLE writer of `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` (`__main__.py`), which `last_pass.py` reads to surface `reconcile_diagnostics` via `rebar bridge status`. The canonical successor is **`rebar bridge fsck`** (the offline binding-drift/discrepancy audit delivered by ticket 3b66 \"Migrate bridge reconcile diagnostics\"). **DECISION:** repoint `_bridge_runner.py`'s `reconcile-check` profile to `(\"rebar\",\"bridge\",\"fsck\")`, AND preserve diagnostic provenance: after removing the legacy writer, `rebar bridge status` MUST continue to surface `reconcile_diagnostics` via the canonical path — EITHER the canonical `bridge fsck` writes/refreshes the `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` report that `last_pass.py` reads, OR `last_pass.py` is migrated to read the canonical fsck diagnostic output. The held-out oracle MUST prove `bridge status` diagnostics parity (same discrepancy/orphan report content) before vs after the change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. The legacy `rebar reconcile` command, its `--mode reconcile-check` route, and its `--filter-local-ids` flag are fully removed from the CLI (registry, parser, help); invoking `rebar reconcile ...` no longer resolves.\n2. `_bridge_runner.py`'s `reconcile-check` profile invokes the canonical `rebar bridge fsck`; no residual `(\"rebar\",\"reconcile\",...)` invocation remains in the runner or any migrated caller.\n3. The LIVE pause sentinel in `_ref_lock.py` (`gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"`) is unchanged; a paused ref-lock blob still strict-decodes and CAS-advances (proven by a regression test in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler`).\n4. `rebar bridge status` continues to surface `reconcile_diagnostics` (discrepancy/orphan report) via the canonical path after the legacy writer is removed; the held-out oracle proves report parity.\n5. CI + probe callers (`reconcile-bridge.yml`, `Jenkinsfile`, both probe scripts) run against the canonical invocation; any retained `reconcile-check` PROFILE/mode label is documented as label-only (invocation migrated).\n6. `docs` + `CHANGELOG.md` record the removal and the canonical migration path.\n\n## Out of scope / deferred\n\n- Engine-internal `filter_local_ids` dead-plumbing removal → follow-up **f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0**.\n- Any change to the `_ref_lock.py` live pause sentinel (Design Decision 2 — preserved unchanged)."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788484013167279870,"uuid":"ff1ab7bb-2c24-4a18-98c9-4a0b3de86954"}